# Always Add Tests With Code Changes

When you change application logic under `lib/`, **add or update unit tests in the same change**. Do not ship behavior-only PRs/diffs without tests.

## Required

- New behavior, bug fixes, and refactors of logic → matching tests under `test/` (mirror `lib/src/` paths)
- Prefer pure unit tests for domain/utils; use `mocktail` + `ProviderContainer` overrides for controllers/orchestrators
- Run `flutter test` for affected tests (or the full suite) before considering the work done
- Reuse helpers in `test/helpers/` (`fixtures.dart`, `mocks.dart`) when possible

## What needs tests

- Core utils, foundation, sync helpers, filter builders
- Domain getters/rules (memberships, cart, payments, stock, roles)
- Orchestrators and controllers with branching business logic
- Extracted pure helpers (prefer extracting hard-to-test private logic)

## Exceptions (no new tests required)

- Generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.mapper.dart`, slang/i18n outputs)
- Pure docs, comments, formatting-only, or asset-only changes
- Trivial one-line wiring with no behavior change (still update tests if existing ones break)

## Layout

```
lib/src/features/pos/domain/sale_payment_status.dart
 → test/features/pos/domain/sale_payment_status_test.dart
```

See `docs/testing.md` for how to run the suite.
